{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-256516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a zero of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,3]\\times [0,1]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}xy-1 \\\\ {y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process that starts with ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,1]^{T}.$\n\n| ${x}_{1}=[$ | {{field-1}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0.5$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of finding the zeros of a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{J}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${J}_{f}({x}_{n})$ is the Jacobian of $f$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the Jacobian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-1) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -2xy & 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -2xy & 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}x & y \\\\ -2xy & 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ -2xy & 3{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}xy-1 \\\\ {y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2(1)(1) & 3(1)^{2}-(1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}(1)(1)-1 \\\\ (1)^{3}-(1)^{2}(1)+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1.5 \\\\ 0.5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256516" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "178dfc7769acdecadf0b8bb9a87eb5c69d9b1f5e8baa97ebfe309f6db6b36f4b"} {"question" "q-256516" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256516" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a zero of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [1,2]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}-6 \\\\ {x}^{3}-3xy+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process that starts with ${x}_{0}=[1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Round your answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n| ${x}_{1}≈[$ | {{field-1}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of finding the zeros of a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{J}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${J}_{f}({x}_{n})$ is the Jacobian of $f$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the Jacobian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{3}-6) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{3}-6) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-3xy+4) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-3xy+4)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x & 3{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-3y & -3x\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}2x & 3{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-3y & -3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}-6 \\\\ {x}^{3}-3xy+4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}2x & 3{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-3y & -3x\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{3}-6 \\\\ {x}^{3}-3xy+4\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2(1) & 3(2)^{2} \\\\ 3(1)^{2}-3(2) & -3(1)\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}(1)^{2}+(2)^{3}-6 \\\\ (1)^{3}-3(1)(2)+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 12 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-3)-12\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{30}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{10} \\\\ \\frac{53}{30}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}0.9 \\\\ 1.767\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "178dfc7769acdecadf0b8bb9a87eb5c69d9b1f5e8baa97ebfe309f6db6b36f4b"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.900"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256561" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.767"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a zero of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[-2,0]\\times [-2,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}xy-1 \\\\ {y}^{3}+3x{y}^{4}+3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process that starts with ${x}_{0}=[-1,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Round your answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n| ${x}_{1}≈[$ | {{field-1}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-0.917$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of finding the zeros of a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{J}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${J}_{f}({x}_{n})$ is the Jacobian of $f$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the Jacobian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy-1) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy-1) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}+3x{y}^{4}+3) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{3}+3x{y}^{4}+3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ 3{y}^{4} & 3{y}^{2}+12x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ 3{y}^{4} & 3{y}^{2}+12x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}xy-1 \\\\ {y}^{3}+3x{y}^{4}+3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ 3{y}^{4} & 3{y}^{2}+12x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}xy-1 \\\\ {y}^{3}+3x{y}^{4}+3\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 3(-1)^{4} & 3(-1)^{2}+12(-1)(-1)^{3}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}(-1)(-1)-1 \\\\ (-1)^{3}+3(-1)(-1)^{4}+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 15\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 15-(-1)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}15 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{13}{12} \\\\ -\\frac{11}{12}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}-1.083 \\\\ -0.917\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256200" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "178dfc7769acdecadf0b8bb9a87eb5c69d9b1f5e8baa97ebfe309f6db6b36f4b"} {"question" "q-256200" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256200" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.083"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we wish to find a zero of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[1,3]\\times [-1,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}+x \\\\ {x}^{3}-{y}^{4}-2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nCalculate one iteration of the Newton-Raphson process that starts with ${x}_{0}=[2,\\,-1]^{T}.$ Round your answer to three decimal places (if needed).\n\n| ${x}_{1}≈[$ | {{field-1}} | $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Newton-Raphson method of finding the zeros of a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{J}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${J}_{f}({x}_{n})$ is the Jacobian of $f$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the Jacobian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}_{f}(x) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}+x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}+x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}-{y}^{4}-2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}-{y}^{4}-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3}+1 & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-2y \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & -4{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3}+1 & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-2y \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & -4{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}+x \\\\ {x}^{3}-{y}^{4}-2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-{[\\begin{aligned}2x{y}^{3}+1 & 3{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-2y \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & -4{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}+x \\\\ {x}^{3}-{y}^{4}-2\\end{aligned}]}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}2(2)(-1)^{3}+1 & 3(2)^{2}(-1)^{2}-2(-1) \\\\ 3(2)^{2} & -4(-1)^{3}\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2}(-1)^{3}-(-1)^{2}+2 \\\\ (2)^{3}-(-1)^{4}-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 14 \\\\ 12 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{(-3)\\cdot 4-14\\cdot 12}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -14 \\\\ -12 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{180}[\\begin{aligned}-82 \\\\ 21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{139}{90} \\\\ -\\frac{53}{60}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ≈[\\begin{aligned}1.544 \\\\ -0.883\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/state.json" "file_sha256" "819ab0222db3e3b1726ac053c7096d647020e50e8fd0826cda532eac644469e7"} {"question" "q-256557" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074434/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "178dfc7769acdecadf0b8bb9a87eb5c69d9b1f5e